    "result_text": "All 255 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS** (0 failures, 0 errors). The stack-trace line in the output is an expected exception logged by a passing negative-path test (`createUserNoRolesFails` reports 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of a new owner whose lower-cased email duplicates any other owner's, responding with **409 Conflict**, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (mirroring the existing telephone-duplicate rule).\n\n**New files:**\n- `RejectDuplicateOwnerEmail.java` \u2014 pipeline step that compares the owner's trimmed, lower-cased email against every existing owner (skipping the owner itself) and throws a checked `DuplicateOwnerEmailException` on a match.\n- `DuplicateOwnerEmailException.java` \u2014 checked exception (`extends Exception`).\n- `DuplicateOwnerEmailExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 escalation handler that responds 409 Conflict with a `ProblemDetail`.\n- `...DuplicateOwnerEmailException.yml` \u2014 escalation wiring.\n\n**Wiring change:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `rejectDuplicateEmail` step (under `transaction` governance) between the telephone-duplicate and household-duplicate steps. It runs after `normalizeEmail`, so the owner's email is already lower-cased; the step also lower-cases defensively for comparison.",
